with less than four weeks until the next  eu summit on monday the general affairs  council will examine the draft agenda  for the heads of state who are expected  to make a final decision on the new  climate and energy policy framework  proposed by the european commission to  move towards a low-carbon economy  eu leaders are also expected to discuss  the economic situation in europe as well  as pressing international issues besides  preparing the ground for the next  european council ministers will also  follow up on the strategic agenda  adopted by eu leaders at their last  meeting in june  they will discuss how to accelerate the  implementation of measures aimed at  fostering growth jobs and  competitiveness in europe  with this aim in mind ministers will  discuss a report prepared by the italian  presidency which reviews progress since  the compact for growth in jobs was  adopted two years ago  finally ministers are expected to adopt  conclusions on the eu strategy for the  adriatic and ionian region  the strategy aims at strengthening  cooperation between the eight  participating countries to the benefit  of 70 million citizens  working together to address common  challenges such as preserving the marine  environment promoting sustainable  tourism and completing transport and  energy networks in the macro region
 

